{"severity":"error","file":"errors/parse_error_11.march","start_line":4,"start_col":4,"end_line":4,"end_col":6,"message":"This `if` (line 4) needs its own `end`: the `end` on line 5 belongs to an outer block.","code":"parse_error","fix":{"kind":"insert","after_line":4,"text":"    end"},"labels":[],"notes":["I only noticed at the end of the file.","`else if` is a nested `if` in the else position, so each `if` needs its own `end`: a two-branch chain ends `end end`, a three-branch chain `end end end`."]}
